{"documentCount":15,"nextId":15,"documentIds":{"0":"docs/pages/getting-started.mdx#get-started","1":"docs/pages/getting-started.mdx#on-chain-integration","2":"docs/pages/what-is-concero.mdx#what-is-concero","3":"docs/pages/what-is-concero.mdx#why-concero","4":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#sending-a-message","5":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#function-signature","6":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#parameters","7":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#evmdstchaindata-structure","8":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#return-value","9":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#usage-example","10":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#important-notes","11":"docs/pages/get-started/sending-a-message.mdx#conceromessagesent-event","12":"docs/pages/js-sdk/installation.mdx#installation","13":"docs/pages/js-sdk/overview.mdx#overview","14":"docs/pages/js-sdk/usage.mdx#usage"},"fieldIds":{"title":0,"titles":1,"text":2},"fieldLength":{"0":[2,1,1],"1":[3,2,1],"2":[4,1,22],"3":[3,4,124],"4":[3,1,36],"5":[2,3,20],"6":[1,3,42],"7":[2,4,33],"8":[2,3,12],"9":[2,3,63],"10":[2,3,23],"11":[2,3,26],"12":[1,1,19],"13":[1,1,1],"14":[1,1,1]},"averageFieldLength":[2.066666666666667,2.2666666666666666,28.266666666666666],"storedFields":{"0":{"href":"/getting-started#get-started","html":"</header>\n","isPage":true,"text":"\n","title":"Get started","titles":[]},"1":{"href":"/getting-started#on-chain-integration","html":"\n<div data-vocs-steps=\"true\"><div data-depth=\"3\"><h3 id=\"\"></h3></div></div>","isPage":false,"text":"\n","title":"On-chain integration","titles":["Get started"]},"2":{"href":"/what-is-concero#what-is-concero","html":"</header>\n<p>Concero is a <strong>fully decentralised</strong> interoperability protocol built to facilitate secure cross-chain value and message transfers in <strong>under 30 seconds</strong>.</p>\n","isPage":true,"text":"\nConcero is a fully decentralised interoperability protocol built to facilitate secure cross-chain value and message transfers in under 30 seconds.\n","title":"What is Concero?","titles":[]},"3":{"href":"/what-is-concero#why-concero","html":"\n<p>Existing cross-chain solutions have to trade security for speed and vice-versa while Concero has been built to be secure and quick at the same time, while being fully decentralised.</p>\n<p>Before designing Concero infrastructure, we have spent a lot of time building, iterating and collecting user feedback about different cross-chain aggregation MVPs. This has been done in order to understand the requirements and solve problems that the end users are facing. After thousands of survey results and usage data points we have boiled down user requirements for cross-chain transactions to three main attributes: Speed, Security and Ease of Use. After trying to look for infrastructure that is able to adhere to these attributes, we found that it does not exist, which laid the foundation behind Concero as the infrastructure.</p>\n<p>We have also set ourselves a strict set of parameters when building this protocol. It had to be fully decentralised, economically feasible for all participants, and fully transparent. As the entire blockchain industry was built on the core principles of transparency, decentralisation and permissionless access, we believe that it is imperative for protocols to adhere to these principles and Concero does just that.</p>","isPage":false,"text":"\nExisting cross-chain solutions have to trade security for speed and vice-versa while Concero has been built to be secure and quick at the same time, while being fully decentralised.\nBefore designing Concero infrastructure, we have spent a lot of time building, iterating and collecting user feedback about different cross-chain aggregation MVPs. This has been done in order to understand the requirements and solve problems that the end users are facing. After thousands of survey results and usage data points we have boiled down user requirements for cross-chain transactions to three main attributes: Speed, Security and Ease of Use. After trying to look for infrastructure that is able to adhere to these attributes, we found that it does not exist, which laid the foundation behind Concero as the infrastructure.\nWe have also set ourselves a strict set of parameters when building this protocol. It had to be fully decentralised, economically feasible for all participants, and fully transparent. As the entire blockchain industry was built on the core principles of transparency, decentralisation and permissionless access, we believe that it is imperative for protocols to adhere to these principles and Concero does just that.","title":"Why Concero?","titles":["What is Concero?"]},"4":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#sending-a-message","html":"</header>\n<p>Concero allows you to send messages from one blockchain to another using the <code>conceroSend</code> function. This enables cross-chain communication for a variety of use cases such as cross-chain token transfers, governance actions, or any custom cross-chain interactions.</p>\n","isPage":true,"text":"\nConcero allows you to send messages from one blockchain to another using the conceroSend function. This enables cross-chain communication for a variety of use cases such as cross-chain token transfers, governance actions, or any custom cross-chain interactions.\n","title":"Sending a Message","titles":[]},"5":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#function-signature","html":"\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">function</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> conceroSend</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    uint24</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> dstChainSelector</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    bool</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> shouldFinaliseSrc</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    address</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> feeToken</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">    ConceroTypes</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">.</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">EvmDstChainData</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> memory</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> dstChainData</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    bytes</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> calldata</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> message</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">external</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> payable</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> returns</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">bytes32</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)</span></span></code></pre>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\nfunction conceroSend(\n    uint24 dstChainSelector,\n    bool shouldFinaliseSrc,\n    address feeToken,\n    ConceroTypes.EvmDstChainData memory dstChainData,\n    bytes calldata message\n) external payable returns (bytes32)\n","title":"Function Signature","titles":["Sending a Message"]},"6":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#parameters","html":"\n<table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>dstChainSelector</code></td><td><code>uint24</code></td><td>Identifier for the destination chain</td></tr><tr><td><code>shouldFinaliseSrc</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>Flag for source chain finality (must be <code>false</code> as it&#x27;s not yet supported)</td></tr><tr><td><code>feeToken</code></td><td><code>address</code></td><td>Token used to pay transaction fees (currently only native tokens are supported, so this must be <code>address(0)</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>dstChainData</code></td><td><code>ConceroTypes.EvmDstChainData</code></td><td>Structure containing destination chain execution parameters</td></tr><tr><td><code>message</code></td><td><code>bytes</code></td><td>The message payload to be sent to the destination chain</td></tr></tbody></table>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\nParameterTypeDescriptiondstChainSelectoruint24Identifier for the destination chainshouldFinaliseSrcboolFlag for source chain finality (must be false as it&#x27;s not yet supported)feeTokenaddressToken used to pay transaction fees (currently only native tokens are supported, so this must be address(0))dstChainDataConceroTypes.EvmDstChainDataStructure containing destination chain execution parametersmessagebytesThe message payload to be sent to the destination chain\n","title":"Parameters","titles":["Sending a Message"]},"7":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#evmdstchaindata-structure","html":"\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">struct</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> EvmDstChainData</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    address</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> receiver;  </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// The contract to receive the message on the destination chain</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    uint256</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> gasLimit;  </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Gas limit for the message execution on the destination chain.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<aside data-callout=\"info\"><p>Make sure <code>gasLimit</code> is sufficient, otherwise the message will revert with an out-of-gas error.</p></aside>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\nstruct EvmDstChainData {\n    address receiver;  // The contract to receive the message on the destination chain\n    uint256 gasLimit;  // Gas limit for the message execution on the destination chain.\n}\nMake sure gasLimit is sufficient, otherwise the message will revert with an out-of-gas error.\n","title":"EvmDstChainData Structure","titles":["Sending a Message","Parameters"]},"8":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#return-value","html":"\n<table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>bytes32</code></td><td>A unique message identifier that can be used to track the message</td></tr></tbody></table>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\nTypeDescriptionbytes32A unique message identifier that can be used to track the message\n","title":"Return Value","titles":["Sending a Message"]},"9":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#usage-example","html":"\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">import</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">IConceroRouter</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">} </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">from</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> &quot;../interfaces/IConceroRouter.sol&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">import</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">ConceroTypes</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">} </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">from</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> &quot;@concero/contracts/interfaces/ConceroTypes.sol&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">import</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">ConceroClient</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">} </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">from</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> &quot;./ConceroClient.sol&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\" data-empty-line=\"true\"> </span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">contract</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> MessageSender</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">  constructor</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">address</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> conceroRouter</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">) </span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">ConceroClient</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(conceroRouter) {}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\" data-empty-line=\"true\"> </span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">  function</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> sendCrossChainMessage</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      uint24</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> dstChainSelector</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      address</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> receiver</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      uint256</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> gasLimit</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      bytes</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> memory</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> messageBody</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">  ) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">external</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> payable</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\" data-empty-line=\"true\"> </span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">      // 1. Quote message fee</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      uint256</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> messageFeeNative </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> IConceroRouter</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(i_conceroRouter).</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">getMessageFee</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        dstChainSelector,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">        false</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Source chain finality not yet supported</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">        address</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">), </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Using native token for fees</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        dstData</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">      );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\" data-empty-line=\"true\"> </span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">      // 2. Prepare destination chain data</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">      ConceroTypes.EvmDstChainData </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">memory</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> dstData </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> ConceroTypes.</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">EvmDstChainData</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">({</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        receiver</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> receiver,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        gasLimit</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> gasLimit</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">      });</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\" data-empty-line=\"true\"> </span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">      // 3. Send the cross-chain message</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">      bytes32</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> messageId </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> IConceroRouter</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(i_conceroRouter).conceroSend{value</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> messageFeeNative}(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        dstChainSelector,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">        false</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Source chain finality not yet supported</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">        address</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">), </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Using native token for fees</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        dstData,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">        messageBody</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">      );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\nimport {IConceroRouter} from &quot;../interfaces/IConceroRouter.sol&quot;;\nimport {ConceroTypes} from &quot;@concero/contracts/interfaces/ConceroTypes.sol&quot;;\nimport {ConceroClient} from &quot;./ConceroClient.sol&quot;;\n \ncontract MessageSender {\n  constructor(address conceroRouter) ConceroClient(conceroRouter) {}\n \n  function sendCrossChainMessage(\n      uint24 dstChainSelector,\n      address receiver,\n      uint256 gasLimit,\n      bytes memory messageBody\n  ) external payable {\n \n      // 1. Quote message fee\n      uint256 messageFeeNative = IConceroRouter(i_conceroRouter).getMessageFee(\n        dstChainSelector,\n        false, // Source chain finality not yet supported\n        address(0), // Using native token for fees\n        dstData\n      );\n \n      // 2. Prepare destination chain data\n      ConceroTypes.EvmDstChainData memory dstData = ConceroTypes.EvmDstChainData({\n        receiver: receiver,\n        gasLimit: gasLimit\n      });\n \n      // 3. Send the cross-chain message\n      bytes32 messageId = IConceroRouter(i_conceroRouter).conceroSend{value: messageFeeNative}(\n        dstChainSelector,\n        false, // Source chain finality not yet supported\n        address(0), // Using native token for fees\n        dstData,\n        messageBody\n      );\n  }\n}\n","title":"Usage Example","titles":["Sending a Message"]},"10":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#important-notes","html":"\n<ul>\n<li>Source chain finality is not yet supported, so <code>shouldFinaliseSrc</code> must be <code>false</code></li>\n<li>Currently only native value is supported for fee payment (ETH, MATIC, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n","isPage":false,"text":"\n\nSource chain finality is not yet supported, so shouldFinaliseSrc must be false\nCurrently only native value is supported for fee payment (ETH, MATIC, etc.)\n\n","title":"Important Notes","titles":["Sending a Message"]},"11":{"href":"/get-started/sending-a-message#conceromessagesent-event","html":"\n<p>When a message is sent, a <code>ConceroMessageSent</code> event is emitted with the following parameters:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">event</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> ConceroMessageSent</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    bytes32</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> indexed</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> messageId</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    uint16</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> version</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    bool</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> shouldFinaliseSrc</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color: